    },
    "name": "dismiss_signal",
    "title": "Dismiss a system signal",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "title": "Execute one command as the Operator or PM",
    },
    "description": "Only the Operator or selected PM, in its own general conversation during an open owner message or answer. The PM may use task_create, task_update, task_labels, task_start, task_cancel, member_update, merge_order and operate. Every other kind is refused with command_not_for_project_manager; with machine access enabled use open_integrator_todo for the integrator, otherwise ask the owners with ask_human. Starts ONE command on the shared operation path, logged as you: {operation}. command is {kind, ...fields of that kind}. workspace_release frees the workspace an unresolved process cleanup keeps reserved without proof that the processes stopped: only on the owner’s explicit request in that conversation, never on a signal by itself; reason is the owner’s stated reason. workspace_release, inbox_resolve, merge, merge_order and invite_create run only when the open request is an owner’s own message or answer; for a queue item or another member’s message the server refuses them (operator_owner_only), so ask the owners with ask_human. On a member’s request task_labels runs with your own label rights: approval and human-only labels are refused. Use operate for configuration, member, session, message and project-pause changes. For the Operator, kinds operate and member_update are refused here with super_operation_unsupported. A K3 effect (deletion, security, cost and permission decisions) is not run: the operation waits in waiting_owner and the owner answers with their own login; after the owner’s yes the server runs it by itself, so do not repeat the call. Machine operations go through the integrator on the owner's request. request_key (1–100 characters of A-Z a-z 0-9 . _ -) names this call within the request: the same key is the same operation and never runs twice; the same key with another command is refused (super_request_conflict). Follow it with get_operation until the state is final.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "command": {
          "additionalProperties": {},
          "description": "The command: kind plus its fields; the fields of each kind are in get_guide with topic "operations".",
          "properties": {
            "kind": {
              "enum": [
                "operate",
                "member_update",
                "invite_create",
                "merge",
                "merge_order",
                "task_create",
                "task_update",
                "task_labels",
                "task_start",
                "task_cancel",
                "inbox_resolve",
                "credential_revoke",
                "workspace_release",
              ],
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "kind",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "request_key": {
          "description": "Names this call within the open request; repeat it only to retry the same call.",
          "maxLength": 100,
          "minLength": 1,
          "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "task_key": {
