  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "List merge checks",
    },
    "description": "Read the project's recorded merge checks (the full check of a merge or of a merge train), newest first: the run time, the workers, the scope and each step with its time and result (a cached step is marked, not timed). The queue wait is shown apart. Filter by card, outcome, kind or period; get_task shows the latest checks of one card.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "kind": {
          "default": "checks",
          "description": "checks (default): the check of a single merge and of a train. diagnose: the per-card diagnosis of a failed train.",
          "enum": [
            "checks",
            "merge",
            "train",
            "diagnose",
            "any",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "limit": {
          "default": 30,
          "maximum": 100,
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "outcome": {
          "default": "any",
          "description": "not_passed: failed, errored, cancelled or still running.",
          "enum": [
            "passed",
            "not_passed",
            "any",
          ],
          "type": "string",
        },
        "since": {
          "description": "Only checks requested at or after this time.",
          "format": "date-time",
          "pattern": "^(?:(?:\\d\\d[2468][048]|\\d\\d[13579][26]|\\d\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\\d|2[0-8])))T(?:(?:[01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d:[0-5]\\d(?:\\.\\d+)?(?:Z|([+-](?:[01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d)))$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "task_key": {
          "description": "Only the checks that included this card.",
          "pattern": "^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]{0,9}-\\d+$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "until": {
          "description": "Only checks requested before this time.",
          "format": "date-time",
          "pattern": "^(?:(?:\\d\\d[2468][048]|\\d\\d[13579][26]|\\d\\d0[48]|[02468][048]00|[13579][26]00)-02-29|\\d{4}-(?:(?:0[13578]|1[02])-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|3[01])|(?:0[469]|11)-(?:0[1-9]|[12]\\d|30)|(?:02)-(?:0[1-9]|1\\d|2[0-8])))T(?:(?:[01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d:[0-5]\\d(?:\\.\\d+)?(?:Z|([+-](?:[01]\\d|2[0-3]):[0-5]\\d)))$",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "list_merge_checks",
    "title": "List merge checks",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "List the recorded system feedback",
    },
    "description": "Only the Operator or the selected PM in its internal coordination session, never an approval continuation; needs no open owner request. The gaps in projectman itself that this project's team recorded earlier, in any state, the latest 50: id, state (new, forwarded, dismissed), title, how many times it occurred and when it was last seen. Look here before record_system_feedback, so the same gap is not recorded twice.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {},
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "list_system_feedback",
    "title": "List the recorded system feedback",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": true,
      "title": "List tasks",
    },
    "description": "Read the project board as a compact list, newest update first. Defaults to open tasks (active, waiting or blocked). Filter by status, stage or assignee; use get_task for details. A theme is marked kind "theme"; it is in no stage, so a stage filter leaves themes out.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "assignee": {
          "description": "Member handle, or "me" for your own tasks.",
          "pattern": "^[a-z0-9][a-z0-9-]{0,31}$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "limit": {
          "default": 50,
          "maximum": 200,
          "minimum": 1,
          "type": "integer",
        },
        "stage": {
          "pattern": "^[a-z][a-z0-9_]{0,31}$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "status": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "const": "open",
              "type": "string",
            },
            {
              "enum": [
                "active",
                "waiting",
                "blocked",
                "done",
                "cancelled",
              ],
              "type": "string",
            },
          ],
          "default": "open",
        },
      },
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "list_tasks",
    "title": "List tasks",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "title": "Mark the offered decision candidates",
    },
    "description": "Only the selected project manager in its internal general conversation, in the owner's own conversation, during an open owner request. Record what the owner said about the candidates you offered: recorded (they said yes and the entry is in the decision log; decision is its number, 1–10 characters), declined (they said no: never offer it again) or skipped (not a decision). All or nothing: one unknown item_id refuses the whole call with not_found. An item already marked can be marked again when the owner asks.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "items": {
          "items": {
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "properties": {
              "decision": {
                "description": "The decision log entry number; only with recorded.",
                "maxLength": 10,
                "minLength": 1,
                "type": "string",
              },
              "item_id": {
                "maxLength": 100,
                "minLength": 1,
                "type": "string",
              },
              "verdict": {
                "enum": [
                  "recorded",
                  "declined",
                  "skipped",
                ],
                "type": "string",
              },
            },
            "required": [
              "item_id",
              "verdict",
            ],
            "type": "object",
          },
          "maxItems": 50,
          "minItems": 1,
          "type": "array",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "items",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "mark_decision_candidates",
    "title": "Mark the offered decision candidates",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "title": "Merge a task",
    },
    "description": "Start merging the card's approved commit into its repository's default branch. The result arrives as a team message. Call again to retry a failed or blocked merge.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "fix_conflict": {
          "description": "After a conflict failure, request a writable merge-fix worktree. Your session restarts when this turn ends.",
          "type": "boolean",
        },
        "resolution": {
          "description": "While fixing: describe what and where you resolved, after committing the mechanical conflict resolution.",
          "maxLength": 2000,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "task_key": {
          "pattern": "^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]{0,9}-\\d+$",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "task_key",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "merge_task",
    "title": "Merge a task",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "title": "Open a todo for the integrator",
    },
    "description": "Only for a member with machine access (an owner switches it on); needs no owner request. Put machine work (an installation, a setting) in the owners' queue: what to do, where, and what is expected. The owner's connected Claude takes the todos from the queue one at a time; use this tool, not a message, for a step that needs its hands. Its answer (done, or handed to the owners with the reason) comes back to you as the asker. When the integrator is not available the owners get it and the result says so. For the project manager: when a stalled, silent, outage or nobody signal needs someone to act, open a todo instead of asking the owners; a card projectman already follows (an open or handed-over obligation) is refused with obligation_tracked, because projectman wakes the responsible and hands the step over itself. A decision only the owners make (cost, deletion, publishing, direction, approval) is not a todo: use ask_human.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "expected": {
          "maxLength": 1000,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "question": {
          "maxLength": 2000,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "task_key": {
          "pattern": "^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]{0,9}-\\d+$",
          "type": "string",
        },
        "what": {
          "maxLength": 2000,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "where": {
          "maxLength": 500,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "question",
        "what",
        "where",
        "expected",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "open_integrator_todo",
    "title": "Open a todo for the integrator",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "title": "Operate the project",
    },
    "description": "Only the Operator or selected PM, in its own general conversation during an open owner request. The PM uses the shared operation path in its own name; K3 effects wait for the owner. Propose a configuration, member, session, message or project pause operation. The server executes immediate changes, requests owner approval for restricted changes, and refuses forbidden changes. Before changing a built-in role, use get_role_configuration, preserve existing instructions and other bundle fields, and send only the affected role in config_patch.roleOverrides. Each supplied bundle replaces that role completely; omitted roles stay unchanged. Set a role to null to reset only that role to built-in defaults; an empty map changes no roles. To add or change one pipeline label (name, color, meaning) send only that label in config_patch.labels, keyed by label id, e.g. {"bug": {"color": "red"}}; omitted fields and all other labels, stages and columns stay unchanged, and null removes the color or meaning. session_stop and message_send require plan (why, impact, reversible). message_send is for non-owner humans, with the exact text the owner approves. Title describes the result in the project language (1–120 characters).",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "operation": {
          "additionalProperties": {},
          "description": "The operation: op plus its fields; the fields of each op are in get_guide with topic "operations".",
          "properties": {
            "op": {
              "enum": [
                "config_patch",
                "member_update",
                "member_hire",
                "member_retire",
                "member_rename",
                "config_revert",
                "session_stop",
                "project_pause",
                "project_resume",
                "message_send",
              ],
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "op",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "plan": {
          "additionalProperties": false,
          "properties": {
            "impact": {
              "maxLength": 500,
              "minLength": 1,
              "type": "string",
            },
            "reversible": {
              "type": "boolean",
            },
            "why": {
              "maxLength": 500,
              "minLength": 1,
              "type": "string",
            },
          },
          "required": [
            "why",
            "impact",
            "reversible",
          ],
          "type": "object",
        },
        "title": {
          "maxLength": 120,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "title",
        "operation",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "operate",
    "title": "Operate the project",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "title": "Move a merge to the front of the queue",
    },
    "description": "One merge runs at a time per repository, in the order the cards were requested; use this to make this card's queued merge go next, e.g. a fix that the queued cards' tests depend on. Only a merge that waits in the queue can move; the merge that runs now is not interrupted. The reason goes on the card's timeline: say who or what it unblocks. A merge already at the front is left as it is (moved: false).",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "reason": {
          "description": "Why this card goes first; it is shown on the timeline.",
          "maxLength": 500,
          "minLength": 1,
          "type": "string",
        },
        "task_key": {
          "pattern": "^[A-Z][A-Z0-9]{0,9}-\\d+$",
          "type": "string",
        },
      },
      "required": [
        "task_key",
        "reason",
      ],
      "type": "object",
    },
    "name": "prioritize_merge",
    "title": "Move a merge to the front of the queue",
  },
  {
    "annotations": {
      "destructiveHint": false,
      "openWorldHint": false,
      "readOnlyHint": false,
      "title": "Propose shared Operator knowledge",
    },
    "description": "The Operator, or the selected project manager in its internal general session, during an open owner message or answer. Propose an agreement replacement, principle put or removal with the current expected_revision. A null principle id gets a server id. Writes nothing until an owner approves in the inbox. Only the Operator’s agreement_replace accepts recommended operations (at most ten); even immediate operations must wait for this approval and protected configuration operations still require a separate approval. Never import principles automatically from memory or documents. What a setting can express (gate, label, permission, priority, complexity limit) is proposed as a setting with operate, not as a principle. Propose a rule only after a repeated failure and name the cards in its reason; refer to a duty or role in rules, not to a member name.",
    "inputSchema": {
      "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "properties": {
        "change": {
          "oneOf": [
